## 6. The one red check — a cross-lane blocker in the shared theme

`feedback/the_scene_mounts_the_theme` fails because
`godot/src/ui/theme/padel_theme.tres` **does not parse**: Godot reports
`Parse Error: Expected 4 arguments for constructor` at line 419. Thirteen palette rows
were written with a 3-argument `Color(r, g, b)`; the `.tres` constructor requires 4
(`r, g, b, a`). Exact lines: **419–429 and 434–435** (`win_green`, `win_ink`, `loss_red`,
`loss_ink`, `trophy_yellow`, `stat_muted`, `item_ink`, `help_muted`, `kbd_border`,
`white`, `challenge_cyan`, `stat_bar`, `stat_bar_rival`).
Mechanical fix: append `, 1` to each. The theme file is the theme lane's (not this
ticket's) — recorded, not edited. The theme mount is the only theme-dependent check in
this audit, so with those 13 lines valid this run has no other candidate red.
